# Argus UI — Local Environment Overrides
# Copy this file to argus-ui/.env.local and uncomment any values you want to override.
# Defaults work for local development — this file is only needed for production,
# Docker, or alternative local setups.

# ─── Hermes server connection ──────────────────────────────────
# Host + ports Argus UI uses to reach Hermes. Defaults match hermes/.env.example:
# host=localhost, ports 3001/3002/3003.

# VITE_HOST=localhost
# VITE_CHAT_PORT=3001
# VITE_BUILD_PORT=3002
# VITE_WARZONE_PORT=3003

# ─── Production hosts (full host per server) ────────────────────
# Override with per-server full hosts for production deployments — e.g. Cloudflare
# tunnel subdomains. Cloudflare is always :443 — no port suffix needed.
# If unset, each server falls back to `${VITE_HOST}:${VITE_<server>_PORT}`.

# VITE_CHAT_HOST=chat.your-domain.com
# VITE_BUILD_HOST=build.your-domain.com
# VITE_WARZONE_HOST=warzone.your-domain.com

# ─── Auth ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sent as `X-Api-Key` header on HTTP requests and `?key=` on WebSocket connections.
# MUST match `API_KEY` in hermes/.env. Leave empty for local dev (no auth).

# VITE_API_KEY=

# ─── Notes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Protocol (http/https, ws/wss) is auto-selected from `window.location.protocol`
# at runtime — no env var needed. If the page is served over HTTPS, WebSocket
# connections use wss automatically.
